 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 20,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "MANDELBULB. One bulb (a sphere with a bud) repeated six times around a core, then the ring repeated once more, smaller and higher. Twelve bulbs on two tiers, from three shapes and two repeat nodes. A noise warp gives every surface its texture.",
    "width": 340
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 560,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "Six inputs land in the lower tier, sight and sound alternating around the ring, mapped straight onto the bulb cells with no retina or cochlea between. Each channel keeps the same cells for the whole run, so a letter lights the same pixels every time it is shown.",
    "width": 340
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "type": "note",
   "x": -380,
   "y": 820,
   "on": true,
   "name": "",
   "params": {
    "text": "Each lower bulb projects into the bulb above it and each upper bulb into the core, so the core is where a letter seen in one bulb meets its name heard in the next. Recurrence is local everywhere: the kernel does not reach between bulbs.",
    "width": 340
   },
   "inputs": []
  },
